      "body": "Validate bad_words token IDs against the model's output vocabulary (logits width) rather than only the tokenizer vocabulary. Multimodal tokenizers can contain input-only placeholder tokens whose IDs exceed the generation logits width, causing out-of-bounds writes in the BadWords Triton kernel.\n- Add model_config parameter to update_from_tokenizer() for model-vocab-aware validation\n- Add output_width bounds check in the BadWords Triton kernel as defense in depth\n- Fix Rust frontend to validate bad_words against model_vocab_size\n- Add regression tests for the vulnerability scenario\n\n<!-- codex-pr-hygiene-validation -->\n## Rebase validation — 2026-10-27\n\nRebased onto upstream main, preserving the original fix and current surrounding behavior. The duplicate audit found no complete merged or open replacement for this PR’s remaining control.\n\nAdapted the existing input-processor call while preserving trace-replay handling.\n\nValidation on macOS CPU: **65 passed**. All applicable changed-file pre-commit checks and `git diff --check` passed.\n\n```bash\nVLLM_TARGET_DEVICE=cpu VLLM_PLUGINS='' PYTHONPATH=. HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1 .venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/test_sampling_params.py -q --tb=short -p no:cacheprovider\n```\n\nNative GPU/RDMA execution and model evaluations were not run during this rebase; required CI and human review remain pending. AI assistance (OpenAI Codex) was used for the conflict resolution and validation.\n",
